What came across: vendor endpoints, contracts, request/response mappings, prices
and captured example responses for the people and company capabilities. What
changed: the file format (theirs is one flat catalog directory, ours splits
vendors from contracts), credential names, capability names where ours already
existed, and the credit pricing, which is DINQ's own.

The port is reproducible: scripts/import_treg.py <treg checkout> catalog

OpenPeopleRouter extracts and adapts the public-provider catalog and routing code
from DINQ PeopleRouter. Hosted account, payment and internal-service code are excluded.
Captured provider responses are not distributed.
